  "contract": {
    "head": "phrase::conditional_law evaluates the registered stage-2 26-coordinate head for one Option<gesture::State>. None masks all four articulation indicators; arbitrary caller values in those four coordinates are ignored. Other values retain their frozen global scaling and masks.",
    "ordinary": "The existing law loops over its state weights and consumes the same per-state kernel, preserving state order and multiplication order. Survival-only calls omit exit logits. Unsupported hazard and unsupported exits retain the previous separate handling.",
    "active_joint": "List::active_phrase requires a known active foreground and five distinct caller-owned compatible extension IDs: stay, new, overlap, reinterpret, inactive. It evaluates a single selected articulation state, not a marginal from the ordinary observer.",
    "admission": "Known raw scores are survival and supported exit scores; inactive requires the caller-supplied observed-low gate. Normalize the positive admitted scores with the existing List::build contract, then apply the 30-second unknown leak once. All-zero support yields unknown mass one. Unsupported exit logits admit only supported stay; an unsupported hazard admits no known option.",
    "clock": "Elapsed endpoints and sample rate generate the hazard duration. Unknown leak uses the integer sample difference divided by sample rate, not subtraction of large floating-point ages. Backward elapsed samples and zero sample rate reject.",
    "identity": "The adapter checks duplicate supplied IDs but does not manufacture or own the compatible path states those IDs name.",
    "difference_from_base": "The joint admitted-list normalization is not the ordinary bootstrap Group::step posterior or its unsupported-mass policy. Sharing the raw head kernel does not equate those different inference updates."
  },
